          "descriptions": [
            {
              "descriptionType": "Abstract",
              "description": "Analysis code and intermediate datasets for Zhu, Liu, Kelp, and Naeger (2026), \"Capturing Time-Resolved Prescribed Fire Emissions with TEMPO Special Observations\", Geophysical Research Letters (manuscript 2026GL125411). tempo-rx-fires-code-v1.0.zip contains the tempo_fires Python package (TEMPO Level-2 NO2 extraction, HRRR wind regridding, wind-aware plume detection, cross-wind line-density integration, EMG fitting, quality control, uncertainty budget, GOES/HMS/FIRMS overlays, and the top-down versus bottom-up comparison) together with the scripts used for every figure and table (MIT License). tempo-rx-fires-data-outputs-v1.0.zip contains the per-scan wind-aligned analysis windows, line densities, and EMG fit results for the QC-passing TEMPO scans of the four prescribed fires (Geneva State Forest, AL, 27 March 2025; Eglin-Blackwater, FL, 28 March 2025; Chattahoochee-Oconee National Forest, GA, 8 April 2026; Fort Stewart, GA, 12 April 2026), the coincident TROPOMI fits, and the CSV tables behind Tables 1, S1, S2, and S3 (CC BY 4.0). tempo-rx-fires-data-inputs-v1.0.zip contains the 5-minute GOES-16/18/19 ABI fire radiative power per burn unit, HMS smoke polygons, MODIS/VIIRS active-fire detections, digitized burn-unit polygons, bottom-up emission tables, and TROPOMI NO2 regridded to the TEMPO grid (CC BY 4.0). Raw TEMPO Level-2 V04 granules (NASA ASDC, doi:10.5067/IS-40e/TEMPO/NO2_L2.004), HRRR analyses, and RAVE v2 files are not redistributed; the extraction and download scripts are included. See README.md inside each archive for reproduction steps."
            }
